<Base title="What to do after a car crash"><article class="wrap article"><h1>What to do after a car crash</h1><p>If anyone is injured or in immediate danger, call 911. Follow emergency responders' instructions.</p><h2>At the scene</h2><p>When safe, exchange contact and insurance details, record the location and circumstances, photograph damage and collect witness contact information. Do not put yourself in danger to gather evidence.</p><h2>After leaving the scene</h2><p>Seek medical attention for injuries or concerning symptoms. Notify your insurer, retain relevant documents and ask the responding agency how to obtain the crash report.</p><h2>Legal questions</h2><p>Consider consulting a licensed attorney if injuries, disputed fault or significant losses are involved. <a href="/attorneys/">Arizona legal resources</a>.</p></article></Base>